1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,164
Kashi's Dev Deepawali: thousands of years old, or only since 1985?

2
00:00:06,164 --> 00:00:10,087
Lakhs of lamps, a river of fire on the ghats.

3
00:00:10,087 --> 00:00:14,570
But what is the real age of this light?

4
00:00:14,570 --> 00:00:19,027
You probably think this tradition is thousands of years old.

5
00:00:19,027 --> 00:00:22,988
That the gods themselves come down to bathe in the Ganga.

6
00:00:22,988 --> 00:00:27,940
But the records say something else. You will be shocked to hear it.

7
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:33,130
Local records say all the ghats were decorated together for the first time in 1985.

8
00:00:33,130 --> 00:00:37,847
It started from Panchganga Ghat. That means just a few decades ago.

9
00:00:37,847 --> 00:00:41,150
So where did this story come from?

10
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:46,089
Because behind this night there is a very old tale.

11
00:00:46,089 --> 00:00:52,125
3 flying cities, in the sky. And that arrow of Shiv,

12
00:00:52,125 --> 00:00:54,320
which burned everything down.

13
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:56,082
So the question is this.

14
00:00:56,082 --> 00:01:01,807
Is this night in Kashi really a remembrance of the burning of Tripur?

15
00:01:01,807 --> 00:01:04,890
Or did Kashi create its own new tradition?

16
00:01:04,890 --> 00:01:09,983
First, the testimony of the scriptures. Then, the coins found beneath the soil.

17
00:01:09,983 --> 00:01:14,058
Then those records, which change the story.

18
00:01:14,058 --> 00:01:19,660
And with every piece of proof, we will clearly tell you whether it is from a scripture or an excavation.

19
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:24,635
And yes, a city named Tripuri really existed.

20
00:01:24,635 --> 00:01:27,123
In the soil of Madhya Pradesh.

21
00:01:27,123 --> 00:01:30,605
This very name was found written on its coins.

22
00:01:30,605 --> 00:01:33,590
But is this the same Tripur?

23
00:01:33,590 --> 00:01:37,199
But the real question begins now.

24
00:01:37,199 --> 00:01:41,324
Where is the oldest testimony of this story?

25
00:01:41,324 --> 00:01:46,480
The answer goes back even before the Mahabharat, straight to the Vedas.

26
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:49,368
The Taittiriya Samhita of the Krishna Yajurveda.

27
00:01:49,368 --> 00:01:55,720
This is considered the oldest written testimony of this story.

28
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:59,763
Samhita means a collection of the Vedas' mantras,

29
00:01:59,763 --> 00:02:02,650
remembered down the generations.

30
00:02:02,650 --> 00:02:07,027
It is written there that the demons had 3 forts.

31
00:02:07,027 --> 00:02:13,045
The lowest of iron. Above it, of silver. And the topmost,

32
00:02:13,045 --> 00:02:15,780
a shining fort of gold.

33
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:19,213
The gods were not able to defeat them.

34
00:02:19,213 --> 00:02:24,606
Then Rudra shot an arrow. Rudra, the Vedic name of Shiv.

35
00:02:24,606 --> 00:02:29,510
The arrow tore through the forts, and the demons were driven away.

36
00:02:29,510 --> 00:02:34,286
But in the Vedas this story is short. Just a few lines.

37
00:02:34,286 --> 00:02:39,062
The real grand scene is found in the Karna Parva of the Mahabharat.

38
00:02:39,062 --> 00:02:43,360
There this tale becomes a whole movie.

39
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:46,878
Karna Parva is that part of the Mahabharat

40
00:02:46,878 --> 00:02:50,396
where Karn becomes the commander. And right there, Duryodhan,

41
00:02:50,396 --> 00:02:54,920
He tells Shalya this old story. So that Shalya,

42
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:56,930
becomes Karn's charioteer.

43
00:02:56,930 --> 00:03:03,264
In the story there are 3 demon brothers. Tarakaksha, Kamalaksha and Vidyunmali.

44
00:03:03,264 --> 00:03:07,065
They have flying cities.

45
00:03:07,065 --> 00:03:12,133
Which keep moving in the sky day and night,

46
00:03:12,133 --> 00:03:15,300
and no one can touch them.

47
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:20,084
The condition was, the cities could fall only when,

48
00:03:20,084 --> 00:03:24,337
they came into a straight line in the sky.

49
00:03:24,337 --> 00:03:28,590
And that moment came very, very rarely.

50
00:03:28,590 --> 00:03:32,704
A special chariot was built for Shiv.

51
00:03:32,704 --> 00:03:37,332
They say the whole universe was in that chariot.

52
00:03:37,332 --> 00:03:41,960
Shiv became Tripurantak, meaning the one who ended Tripur.

53
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:45,177
As soon as Shiv stood up with the bow,

54
00:03:45,177 --> 00:03:49,774
the cities lined up straight. At that very moment 1 arrow was fired.

55
00:03:49,774 --> 00:03:54,370
And in no time, everything turned into fire.

56
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:58,775
But what does this story have to do with the night of Kashi?

57
00:03:58,775 --> 00:04:01,978
Is Dev Deepawali written anywhere in the scriptures?

58
00:04:01,978 --> 00:04:03,980
Here comes the first twist.

59
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:08,719
In the Skanda Purana, the full moon of the month of Kartik is special.

60
00:04:08,719 --> 00:04:12,931
Purana means a book of old stories and rules.

61
00:04:12,931 --> 00:04:17,670
It is called Tripuri Purnima, meaning the full moon of Tripur.

62
00:04:17,670 --> 00:04:22,774
Special acts are prescribed for this day. Kartik snan,

63
00:04:22,774 --> 00:04:26,347
meaning a holy bath in the river. And deepdan,

64
00:04:26,347 --> 00:04:29,920
meaning lighting a lamp and offering it to God.

65
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:34,691
Note that here the talk is about each devotee's own lamp.

66
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:38,161
A festival where the whole city is decorated together?

67
00:04:38,161 --> 00:04:40,330
That is a completely different question.

68
00:04:40,330 --> 00:04:46,675
There is another old tradition, Akashdeep. On a long bamboo pole,

69
00:04:46,675 --> 00:04:53,020
a lamp inside a basket. Burning at a height for the whole month of Kartik.

70
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:57,529
It is mentioned in the Kartik Mahatmya of the Skanda Purana.

71
00:04:57,529 --> 00:05:01,538
Mahatmya means a description of the greatness of something.

72
00:05:01,538 --> 00:05:04,544
This lamp is to please Vishnu,

73
00:05:04,544 --> 00:05:07,550
and for the peace of ancestors.

74
00:05:07,550 --> 00:05:11,970
So the connection of lamps with Kashi is very old.

75
00:05:11,970 --> 00:05:16,391
But that lamp was alone, on the roof of a house,

76
00:05:16,391 --> 00:05:20,320
or at the edge of a ghat. Not a crowded festival.

77
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:23,870
Then comes Kashi's most beloved belief.

78
00:05:23,870 --> 00:05:28,308
On Kartik Purnima, 33 crore gods descend to earth.

79
00:05:28,308 --> 00:05:30,970
Only to bathe in the Ganga.

80
00:05:30,970 --> 00:05:35,867
They celebrate Shiv's victory over Tripurasur.

81
00:05:35,867 --> 00:05:40,274
That's how it got its name, Dev Deepawali, meaning the Diwali of the gods.

82
00:05:40,274 --> 00:05:45,660
This is the folk belief of Kashi, passed down from generation to generation.

83
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:49,566
The story is in the Vedas, the tradition is in the Puranas.

84
00:05:49,566 --> 00:05:53,906
But was there ever a real city called Tripur?

85
00:05:53,906 --> 00:05:56,510
The answer was found in an excavation.

86
00:05:56,510 --> 00:06:01,271
Near Jabalpur in Madhya Pradesh, there is a village, Tewar.

87
00:06:01,271 --> 00:06:04,127
There seems to be nothing special about the name.

88
00:06:04,127 --> 00:06:07,460
But beneath the land around it,

89
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:09,840
an ancient city lies asleep.

90
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:13,546
ASI, that is, the Archaeological Survey of India.

91
00:06:13,546 --> 00:06:18,487
The government body that looks after the country's old heritage.

92
00:06:18,487 --> 00:06:23,429
Its excavation showed that this is the ancient Tripuri.

93
00:06:23,429 --> 00:06:28,370
Excavation means slowly digging the earth to bring out history.

94
00:06:28,370 --> 00:06:31,756
How old is this settlement? According to the ASI,

95
00:06:31,756 --> 00:06:36,411
its roots are very old. Going back to the last phase of the Chalcolithic age.

96
00:06:36,411 --> 00:06:40,220
That is, when people used copper and stone together.

97
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:43,884
And then coins were found. Copper coins.

98
00:06:43,884 --> 00:06:49,642
The name of the city was written on them, Tirpuri. In the Prakrit language,

99
00:06:49,642 --> 00:06:53,830
in the Brahmi script. This is the biggest proof.

100
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:59,296
Brahmi is one of the oldest scripts of India.

101
00:06:59,296 --> 00:07:03,668
Prakrit is the spoken language of that time.

102
00:07:03,668 --> 00:07:09,680
And the age of the coins? 2nd century BCE, or even earlier.

103
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:13,806
Think about the Tripur that the Mahabharat talks about.

104
00:07:13,806 --> 00:07:18,964
And the coins found in the ground, with Tirpuri written on them.

105
00:07:18,964 --> 00:07:23,090
Is this the same Tripur? This is where we must be careful.

106
00:07:23,090 --> 00:07:27,833
The coins only tell us that a city named Tripuri existed.

107
00:07:27,833 --> 00:07:30,851
People lived there and did trade.

108
00:07:30,851 --> 00:07:34,300
The soil gives no proof of flying forts.

109
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:38,759
The ASI started excavating in Tewar again, in 2021.

110
00:07:38,759 --> 00:07:42,326
This time even more things came out of the ground.

111
00:07:42,326 --> 00:07:47,230
And these things point toward a big city.

112
00:07:47,230 --> 00:07:52,325
Sandstone pillars were found. Sandstone,

113
00:07:52,325 --> 00:07:56,853
that same reddish-brown stone. Along with it, a brick wall,

114
00:07:56,853 --> 00:08:03,080
and things from olden times. It is all slowly coming out.

115
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:07,532
The ASI says people settled here for a long time.

116
00:08:07,532 --> 00:08:12,973
This was an organized city. But the work is not finished yet.

117
00:08:12,973 --> 00:08:16,930
The pillars have not even been fully uncovered yet.

118
00:08:16,930 --> 00:08:19,452
So Tripuri was a real city.

119
00:08:19,452 --> 00:08:21,974
But Dev Deepawali is not held in Tripuri,

120
00:08:21,974 --> 00:08:24,917
it is held on the Ganga ghats of Kashi.

121
00:08:24,917 --> 00:08:28,700
And the age of those ghats? Here comes the next twist.

122
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:34,738
The ghats of Varanasi, the stone steps going down to the river.

123
00:08:34,738 --> 00:08:40,171
There are 84 ghats in all. Looking at the pictures, you think,

124
00:08:40,171 --> 00:08:43,190
they must be thousands of years old.

125
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:48,519
But the tentative list of ASI and UNESCO says something different.

126
00:08:48,519 --> 00:08:51,911
Most of the ghats were rebuilt after 1700.

127
00:08:51,911 --> 00:08:57,240
That means the stones you touch today are not that old.

128
00:08:57,240 --> 00:09:02,217
At that time Kashi was under the influence of the Maratha empire.

129
00:09:02,217 --> 00:09:08,299
The ghats were built by the Marathas, Scindia, Holkar, Bhonsle and Peshwas.

130
00:09:08,299 --> 00:09:12,170
They laid stone steps along the riverbank.

131
00:09:12,170 --> 00:09:15,092
This does not mean Kashi is new.

132
00:09:15,092 --> 00:09:18,013
Worship on the banks of the Ganga can be very old.

133
00:09:18,013 --> 00:09:21,300
It's just that today's stone steps are from later.

134
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:26,369
According to the scriptures, the month of Kartik is special.

135
00:09:26,369 --> 00:09:30,875
People would bathe in the morning and hang Akashdeep lamps high up in baskets.

136
00:09:30,875 --> 00:09:37,070
But the sea of lamps like today? Its story is completely different.

137
00:09:37,070 --> 00:09:41,720
Now think. The scriptures mention deepdan. There is a tradition of Akashdeep.

138
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:44,045
The ghats were made of solid stone later.

139
00:09:44,045 --> 00:09:49,160
So when were lamps first lit on all the ghats together?

140
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:53,594
And that story begins at Panchganga Ghat.

141
00:09:53,594 --> 00:09:57,536
With a date that is quite recent.

142
00:09:57,536 --> 00:10:01,970
But even the records don't agree on one thing.

143
00:10:01,970 --> 00:10:07,564
According to local records, collective Dev Deepawali began in 1985.

144
00:10:07,564 --> 00:10:12,649
Collective means the people of the whole ghat celebrating together.

145
00:10:12,649 --> 00:10:15,700
Not a separate lamp for each house.

146
00:10:15,700 --> 00:10:20,513
The place was Panchganga Ghat, one of Kashi's old ghats.

147
00:10:20,513 --> 00:10:24,014
There people together decorated the steps with lamps.

148
00:10:24,014 --> 00:10:28,390
And before long, the word spread across the whole city.

149
00:10:28,390 --> 00:10:33,091
Then in 1991 the festival spread to Dashashwamedh Ghat.

150
00:10:33,091 --> 00:10:36,616
There it took an even bigger form.

151
00:10:36,616 --> 00:10:43,080
Slowly the other ghats joined too. This is the look of it today.

152
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:48,757
But here the records differ. One source says,

153
00:10:48,757 --> 00:10:52,731
it began in 1991. At Dashashwamedh Ghat,

154
00:10:52,731 --> 00:10:55,570
it was done by a local priest.

155
00:10:55,570 --> 00:11:00,269
People knew him by the name Babu Maharaj,

156
00:11:00,269 --> 00:11:03,401
Pandit Kishori Raman Dubey. On the other hand,

157
00:11:03,401 --> 00:11:08,100
some records mention 1985 and Panchganga.

158
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:13,164
So opinions differ on where and when it began.

159
00:11:13,164 --> 00:11:16,386
But everyone agrees on one thing.

160
00:11:16,386 --> 00:11:20,990
This collective form is a few decades old, not thousands of years.

161
00:11:20,990 --> 00:11:24,643
So we've got half the answer to the first question.

162
00:11:24,643 --> 00:11:27,840
The story of Shiva is in the ancient texts.

163
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:30,580
Bathing and lighting lamps are also ancient.

164
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:33,320
The light on all the ghats is new.

165
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:36,993
Does that make the tradition smaller? Not at all.

166
00:11:36,993 --> 00:11:40,257
Kashi gave the old story a new form.

167
00:11:40,257 --> 00:11:43,930
Every tradition, at some point, was new.

168
00:11:43,930 --> 00:11:47,013
But now the deepest question remains.

169
00:11:47,013 --> 00:11:50,096
How did the cities line up in the sky?

170
00:11:50,096 --> 00:11:54,500
Did anyone really see something in the sky?

171
00:11:54,500 --> 00:12:00,240
Remember the condition in the Mahabharat. The cities could burn only when

172
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:05,979
they came into a line. And that rarely happened.

173
00:12:05,979 --> 00:12:09,110
This is exactly what attracts scholars.

174
00:12:09,110 --> 00:12:14,643
Some scholars say it could be a conjunction of planets.

175
00:12:14,643 --> 00:12:18,165
Conjunction means when planets in the sky appear close together,

176
00:12:18,165 --> 00:12:20,680
in one line.

177
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:27,753
Archaeoastronomy is the science of finding information about the sky in old texts and buildings.

178
00:12:27,753 --> 00:12:32,106
Some people connected to this ask the same thing.

179
00:12:32,106 --> 00:12:35,370
Did our ancestors see something?

180
00:12:35,370 --> 00:12:38,980
Some others make a different guess.

181
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:42,591
Maybe a meteor was seen falling.

182
00:12:42,591 --> 00:12:46,201
A meteor is a burning stone falling from the sky,

183
00:12:46,201 --> 00:12:48,780
what we call a shooting star.

184
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:54,064
But many scholars of religion and texts think very differently.

185
00:12:54,064 --> 00:12:57,427
For them, this story is an allegory.

186
00:12:57,427 --> 00:13:01,270
An allegory means giving a deep lesson through a story.

187
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:05,810
According to them, this is the language of the Vedic yagya.

188
00:13:05,810 --> 00:13:10,349
Or a symbol of the end of the universe and a new beginning.

189
00:13:10,349 --> 00:13:13,880
That is, it's not a story of the sky, but of the mind.

190
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:18,817
Who is right? Nobody has been able to decide so far.

191
00:13:18,817 --> 00:13:21,779
The sky theory has not been proven.

192
00:13:21,779 --> 00:13:27,210
And the allegory view is also just one way of reading.

193
00:13:27,210 --> 00:13:29,554
So what don't we know yet?

194
00:13:29,554 --> 00:13:35,179
We don't know where the story of the 3 flying cities came from.

195
00:13:35,179 --> 00:13:38,460
From looking at the sky, or from the language of yagya.

196
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:43,639
The link between Tewar's Tripuri and this story is also not clear.

197
00:13:43,639 --> 00:13:46,934
The names match, but the proof is incomplete.

198
00:13:46,934 --> 00:13:50,230
And the excavation there is not yet complete.

199
00:13:50,230 --> 00:13:56,048
And where was it lit on the first evening of Dev Deepawali, Panchganga or Dashashwamedh?

200
00:13:56,048 --> 00:13:59,222
The records don't speak in one voice.

201
00:13:59,222 --> 00:14:05,040
Maybe the elders of Kashi still remember that night even today.

202
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:09,828
But what is known, you can see for yourself.

203
00:14:09,828 --> 00:14:13,658
Straight with your own eyes. Come, let's go to Kashi.

204
00:14:13,658 --> 00:14:17,010
And then all the way to the soil of Tewar.

205
00:14:17,010 --> 00:14:22,048
On the evening of Kartik Purnima, stand on the ghats of Kashi.

206
00:14:22,048 --> 00:14:26,582
Stone steps, laid down in the time of the Marathas.

207
00:14:26,582 --> 00:14:31,620
On them burn lamps, a gift of the last few decades.

208
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:35,625
See the morning Kartik bath in the Ganga.

209
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:40,201
And look for the Akashdeep, the lamps in baskets, on tall bamboo poles.

210
00:14:40,201 --> 00:14:45,350
This is the part that is written in the scriptures.

211
00:14:45,350 --> 00:14:50,368
And if you want to touch the soil of history, then go to Tewar.

212
00:14:50,368 --> 00:14:55,887
About 2 km from Tewar village, the site of ancient Tripuri.

213
00:14:55,887 --> 00:14:59,400
Where the ASI dug out pillars and walls.

214
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:03,502
So, back to the first question. Shiv burned Tripur,

215
00:15:03,502 --> 00:15:08,515
this is a story from the scriptures. And Kashi, on that story,

216
00:15:08,515 --> 00:15:11,250
created a new tradition of lamps.

217
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:14,868
In the next video we will go to Pushkar,

218
00:15:14,868 --> 00:15:22,105
where a fair is held on Kartik Purnima. But first tell me.

219
00:15:22,105 --> 00:15:30,066
Have you seen Dev Deepawali in Kashi, or only in pictures?
